@startuml selma_directive_lifecycle
' ============================================================
' Selma — Directive Lifecycle State Machine
' Source:  SPECIFICATION.md §2.2, §2.2.4, §2.3, §2.5
'          User_Stories.md S-01, S-02, S-03, S-08, S-19, S-20, S-26
' C4:      Application Service + Directives Adapter → directive_store
'          Hermetic Compiler on every publish / identity op
' Contract: 8.2.4
'
' Dual identity:
'   lineage_id   = immutable root (Machine ID at creation)
'   execution_id = active node identity (changes on fork/merge/split)
' Status enum (schema): draft | active | deprecated | superseded
' ============================================================

title Selma — Directive Lifecycle FSM\n<size:12><i>Status path + dual-identity operations · parent deprecation · hermetic recompile</i></size>

!include ./common/sm_styles.puml

[*] --> Draft : <b>directive.create</b>\nactor: Regulatory Official\nlineage_id := Machine ID\nexecution_id := lineage_id (1:1)\nauthored_by := actor\nstory: S-01

state "Draft" as Draft #B9770E : **mutable drafting**\nnot yet binding in production CG-IR\n**allowed** modify · publish\n**forbidden** retire · fork · merge · split
state "Active" as Active #2C6E49 : **published & operational**\npresent in CG-IR snapshot\n**allowed** modify · retire · supersede\n**allowed** fork · merge · split
state "Deprecated" as Deprecated #4A4A4A : **retired / absorbed**\naudit trail preserved\nCG-IR nodes marked deprecated\n**allowed** restore only
state "Superseded" as Superseded #4A4A4A : **replaced by successor**\nmetadata.migration.superseded_by\nMUST reference active or draft id\n**forbidden** restore without\nnew successor governance

' ---------- Status transitions ----------
Draft --> Active : <b>directive.modify (publish)</b>\n+ hermetic compile success\nnew CG-IR snapshot\nstory: S-01 / S-02
Draft --> Draft : <b>directive.modify (revision)</b>\nlineage_id unchanged\nexecution_id unchanged\nstory: S-02

Active --> Active : <b>directive.modify (revision)</b>\nwrite lock · incremental compile\nsame lineage_id + execution_id\nstory: S-02
Active --> Deprecated : <b>directive.retire</b>\nreason recorded\nCG-IR nodes marked deprecated\nstory: S-03
Active --> Superseded : <b>supersede</b>\nmetadata.migration.superseded_by set\nsuccessor compile-validated\n§2.2.4

Deprecated --> Draft : <b>directive.restore</b>\ntarget revision copied\nlineage_id preserved\nmust recompile to re-activate\nstory: S-08

' ---------- Identity operations (spawn new instances; parent deprecates) ----------
state "Fork Children\n(new instances)" as ForkChildren #1B7A6E : 2 new execution_ids\nshared lineage_id\nlineage.operation = fork\nchildren Draft then Active\nvia hermetic compile
state "Merge Result\n(new instance)" as MergeResult #1B7A6E : lineage_id = MIN(parents) lex\nexecution_id = lineage_id + "-M" +\nSHA-256(...)[0:16]\nboth parents Deprecated
state "Split Children\n(new instances)" as SplitChildren #1B7A6E : N new execution_ids\nshared lineage_id\nlineage.operation = split\nparent Deprecated

Active --> ForkChildren : <b>directive.fork</b>\n[capability: directive.fork]\nparent becomes Deprecated\nstory: S-19
Active --> MergeResult : <b>directive.merge</b>\n[capability: directive.merge]\nbinary merge only (v8.2.x)\nstory: S-20
Active --> SplitChildren : <b>directive.split</b>\n[capability: directive.split]\nparent becomes Deprecated\nstory: S-26

ForkChildren --> Active : children publish compile\n(new execution_id instances)
MergeResult --> Active : merged rule publish compile\n(new execution_id instance)
SplitChildren --> Active : children publish compile\n(new execution_id instances)

Superseded --> [*]
Deprecated --> [*] : if not restored

note left of Draft
  **Identity contract (§2.3)**
  · lineage_id assigned once, never reassigned
  · Machine ID ↔ lineage root bijective at
    root-assignment level
  · after fork/split, multiple active rules may
    share lineage_id with distinct execution_ids
end note

note right of Active
  **Lineage DAG gates (compile-time §2.2.3)**
  · acyclicity (DFS)
  · parent existence + temporal ordering
  · fork/split: exactly 1 parent
  · merge: exactly 2 parents
  · depth ≤ 64 · no self-reference
  · creator_provenance inheritance:
    fork/split inherit; merge = sorted union
end note

note bottom of MergeResult
  **Deterministic merge (§2.2.2)**
  lineage_id := MIN(parent_a, parent_b)
  Non-surviving parent preserved only in
  lineage.parent_lineage_ids + optional
  metadata.migration.merge_provenance.
  Concurrency: exclusive write lock on
  Directive Graph (SPEC §3.4); no lock-type
  inversion with compilation read lock.
end note

@enduml
